---
/**
 * Text Diff tool page.
 */
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import TextDiff from '../../components/tools/TextDiff';
---

<ToolLayout slug="text-diff">
  <TextDiff client:load />

  <Fragment slot="about">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">01 · The Problem</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Most online diff tools answer the wrong question. They report line additions and
          deletions, scoring a one-word edit inside a reflowed paragraph as a total replacement.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Goal: Accurate character-level similarity ratios and fine-grained word diffing.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">02 · Myers + Word Pairing</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Line alignment runs Myers' greedy edit-graph walk (from <code>git diff</code>).
          Delete/insert runs are paired into modified blocks and diffed at the word level.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Optimization: Common prefix/suffix stripping + line interning for millisecond speed.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">03 · Semantic Gap</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Lexical similarity and semantic meaning diverge on paraphrases and negations. The semantic
          engine compares TF-IDF or model embeddings to highlight meaning shifts.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Actionable: Alignment table maps paragraph-to-paragraph shifts.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hud-card border-warn mt-6 border-l-2 p-5">
      <h3 class="eyebrow text-warn mb-3">Operational Limits & Edge Cases</h3>
      <ul class="text-muted grid gap-3 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:grid-cols-2">
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>2,000 Edit Threshold:</strong> Past 2,000 edits, minimal alignment stops and falls
            back to block replacement. Similarity figures remain exact.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>No Move Tracking:</strong> Relocating a block appears as an insertion and deletion
            without cross-position linking.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>Embedding Negation Blindspot:</strong> Embedding models often score negations as
            similar subject matter. Check the lexical diff for flipped words.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>Cosine Calibration:</strong> Unrelated embeddings cluster around 0.65. Use the interpreted
            bands or angular distance for realistic scale.</span
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
